{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1764642,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Operations Redefined 2026 - Evaluated by KPMG India","festival_id":null,"organization_id":14609,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-11-28T17:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/operations-redefined-2026-evaluated-by-kpmg-india-nmims-indore-1764642","region":"online","details":"<p><strong>Overview<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Sharpen your strategic thinking and take on real-world operational problems at the Operations Unstop Challenge 2026. This event gives participants a chance to spot inefficiencies, design innovative solutions, and build business strategies that create real impact.<\/p>\n<p><strong>General Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The competition consists of three elimination rounds.<\/li>\n<li>Each team must have 2-3 members. Participants can come from B-schools as well as other colleges\/universities, and the challenge is also open to current research scholars, post-doctoral fellows, and working professionals across relevant disciplines.<\/li>\n<li>In case of any discrepancy, the organizers' decision will be final, and no further queries will be entertained.<\/li>\n<li>Any team found violating the rules will be disqualified from the competition.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Online Quiz<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The quiz consists of 40 questions to be completed within 25 minutes.<\/li>\n<li>Shortlisting will be based on both accuracy and speed of completion.<\/li>\n<li>The quiz can only be accessed during the scheduled time slot on the Unstop platform.<\/li>\n<li>Only the team leader will have access to attempt the quiz.<\/li>\n<li>Once a question is answered and you move forward, you cannot go back to change previous responses navigation is disabled.<\/li>\n<li>Screen sharing and switching between browser tabs\/windows is not permitted during the quiz.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Case Study Submission<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must submit one PowerPoint presentation (maximum 5 slides, excluding the title, appendix, and cover page) in PPT or PDF format through Unstop.<\/li>\n<li>The submission deadline will be strictly enforced, and late entries will not be accepted.<\/li>\n<li>Files must follow this naming format: Case_CollegeName_TeamName (for example, Case_NMIMS_Alpha).<\/li>\n<li>Teams should use the primary data provided in the case and cite any secondary sources referenced.<\/li>\n<li>The presentation should clearly address the problem statement and propose operational, technological, and financial solutions, along with the assumptions made.<\/li>\n<li>An implementation plan outlining the resources required must also be included.<\/li>\n<li>Judging criteria will center on innovation and creativity, feasibility of the solution, scalability and impact, analytical rigor, and presentation clarity.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 3: On-Campus Pitch Presentation<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams that make it through will pitch their solutions to a judging panel comprising professors and industry experts from KPMG India.<\/li>\n<li>Each team presents, followed by a Q&amp;A round.<\/li>\n<li>Winners will be declared through email and the event's official social media channels.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":4785400,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-02T00:55:56+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-05T17:00:09+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"OSYUERs","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_relea